Package: AssignParents
Type: Package
Title: Post-Denoising ASV Refinement for Metabarcoding Workflows
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person(
        given = "Peter",
        family = "Oppenheimer",
        email = "pjoppenh@ncsu.edu",
        role = c("aut", "cre"),
        comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-0589-466X")
    )
Description: Provides tools for post-denoising refinement of amplicon
    sequence variant tables from metabarcoding workflows. AssignParents
    reconciles high-confidence CLEAN ASV tables with permissive DIRTY ASV
    tables by identifying likely daughter ASVs of parent ASVs using sequence
    identity, presence similarity, abundance similarity, and dominance-based
    filters. Assigned daughter ASV reads are collapsed into parent ASVs while
    preserving total read counts. The package is intended to reduce residual
    denoising artifacts and Phred-score-related biases in downstream ecological
    and quantitative metabarcoding analyses.
